detail.otherInfo:
1.	Passed Matriculation from Mount Carmel School, Bhagalpur, Bihar;  
2.	Was the head of the School Cabinet;  
3.	Topped in all the examinations in Schools & Colleges;  
4.	Graduated in English (Hon.) from Bhagalpur University;  
5.	Cleared I.A.S. Examination in 1994 in the first attempt;  
6.	Adjudged as the best speaker in “Inter College Debate Competition” in New Delhi;  
7.	Adjudged as best actor and best debater in the College for three consecutive years;  
8.	Served as District Magistrate & Collector in four districts of Odisha such as Khordha, Nuapada, Koraput, and Bargarh  
9.	Served the Government  of Odisha in various administrative capacities such as :  
i)	Director, Social Welfare,  
ii)	Director, Mission Shakti for 4 years,
iii)	Municipal Commissioner, Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation for close to 4 years, 
iv)	Secretary, Education (Both in School & Mass Education Department & Higher Education Department),  
v)	Secretary, Rural Development, 
vi)	Secretary Handlooms & Textiles Department;  
10.	Served in the Government of India :  
 As Joint Secretary in handling MGNREGS (Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme) in the Ministry of Rural Development of GOI from 2013-2018. The MGNREGS is considered as the largest anti poverty programme in the world; 
11.	Inspired by the ideals of public service and a larger platform to serve the people, she sought retirement from I.A.S and joined B.J.P in November 2018;  
12.	Varied interests-Reading, writing, travelling, connecting with people  and interior decoration

detail.social:
Gonda is amongst the most backward district of UP with a very low literacy rate;

To encourage education among the masses in this rural area, have set up a girl`s Intermediate college and also a Post Graduate College for higher studies; Currently manage 4 Educational institutes; have actively fought against the education mafia in this district and succeeded in having strict curbs put on the rampant practice of organized cheating /mass copying during Board Exams;
To enhance rural livelihood of local fishermen , was instrumental in setting up a Pilot Project of Cage culture of fish rearing under the aegis of Ford Foundation of India, in 1988, the first of its kind in the country;
Regularly held workshops with local fishermen co-operatives to impart latest information on fish rearing and fish breeding techniques and also provided technical knowledge how to farmers to set up their own fish breeding hatcheries

